(* A cart belongs to whoever is shopping; a catalogue belongs to the shop.
   ARO-0094 — the scope is declared once, here, and no statement below
   restates it. *)

(Application-Start: Shop) {
    Declare the <catalogue-repository> with { scope: "application" }.
    Declare the <cart-repository>      with { scope: "session" }.
    Declare the <sessions-repository>  with { scope: "application" }.

    (* Local development only. A session cookie is not issued over plain HTTP
       at all, so turning that off is something you write down rather than
       something you fall into. Idle expiry (30 minutes) and absolute expiry
       (12 hours) keep their defaults; they are separate because the second is
       the one a stolen cookie cannot refresh away. *)
    Configure the <session: secure> with false.

    Store the <hat> into the <catalogue-repository> with { id: "hat", price: 12 }.
    Store the <boot> into the <catalogue-repository> with { id: "boot", price: 40 }.

    Start the <http-server> with <contract>.
    Keepalive the <application> for the <events>.
    Return an <OK: status> for the <startup>.
}
